# Shared, non-secret Cloud Functions config (committed). Loaded for EVERY project; functions/.env.<projectId>
# (.env.shamyra-web, .env.kindflames-test) is layered on top by the Firebase CLI at deploy time and in the
# emulator. Secrets (STRIPE_SECRET_KEY, STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET, PAYPAL_*, RESEND_API_KEY) are NOT here: they live
# in Secret Manager per project (`firebase functions:secrets:set NAME -P prod|test`). See docs/ENVIRONMENTS.md.
#
# Keys read by functions/index.js (code defaults in brackets):
#   SITE_URL          public origin of the storefront [https://kindflames.com]
#   IS_PRODUCTION     true/false: real money, live PayPal, real customers [true]
#   EXTRA_ORIGINS     comma list of extra browser origins allowed to call checkout (localhost ports,
#                     <projectId>.web.app and <projectId>.firebaseapp.com are always allowed) []
#   ADMIN_EMAILS      comma list; ensureAdmin grants the admin claim to these sign-ins []
#   OWNER_EMAIL       where owner alerts go [first ADMIN_EMAILS entry]
#   FROM_EMAIL        Resend sender ["Kind Flames <orders@kindflames.com>"]
#   REPLY_TO          Resend reply-to [hello@kindflames.com]
#   RESEND_AUDIENCE_ID  optional; marketing.js creates one when unset
ADMIN_EMAILS=prashant0268@gmail.com
OWNER_EMAIL=prashant0268@gmail.com
FROM_EMAIL=Kind Flames <orders@kindflames.com>
REPLY_TO=hello@kindflames.com
